 # Marching Cubes Lookup Tables
 
-Also called: Edge Table, Lorensen and Cline Lookup Tables, MC Case Table, MC Lookup Table, Marching Cubes (GPU Lookup Table Implementation), Marching Cubes Triangle Table, Paul Bourke's table, Precalculated lookup table for Marching Cubes, Tri Table, triangleTable
+Also called: MC Lookup Table, Marching Cubes Triangle Table, Tri Table, Lorensen and Cline Lookup Tables, Paul Bourke's table, Precalculated lookup table for Marching Cubes
 
 ## Overview
-Marching Cubes Lookup Tables are precomputed data structures that map the 256 possible binary configurations of a voxel's corner signs (relative to an isovalue) to the specific edges intersected by the isosurface and the resulting triangle vertex indices [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. This method solves the problem of determining mesh topology without runtime branching logic, allowing for efficient, branchless traversal on both CPU and GPU architectures [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Dual Contouring](778-dual-contouring.md), which optimizes for vertex placement and normal accuracy, or [Surface Nets](921-surface-nets.md), which uses a different topological approach, the Lookup Table method strictly follows the original Lorensen and Cline triangulation, prioritizing simplicity and topological consistency over geometric optimality [S2, S3, unofficial].
